Unlock with the AIDL Gatekeeper and other protectors

On rothko (HyperOS 3, Android 16) TWRP failed every pattern:
- The active protector uses Weaver: android.hardware.weaver-service.nxp on
  the NXP eSE. It talks through OMAPI (android.se.omapi), a service of the
  SecureElement app, so it cannot run in recovery.
- The phone also keeps a Gatekeeper protector (.pwd with a 58-byte handle,
  plus .secdis) for the same synthetic password. Gatekeeper is AIDL only
  (gatekeeper-service.mitee), but TWRP only spoke the HIDL @1.0 HAL.

Use the AIDL Gatekeeper when no HIDL one is registered. When the active
protector fails, try every protector that has Gatekeeper data.

unwrapSyntheticPasswordBlob re-read the active sp-handle from locksettings.db
for the keystore alias, so it decrypted the fallback protector's spblob with
the Weaver protector's key and finish() failed. Use the handle we are trying.

